2014's divergent a movie about a  futuristic version of chicago  boasts a bunch of major stars some have  gone  on to break out into stardom while  others have continued  their stellar work just under the radar  let's take a look  at what they're up to today as tris  pryor  divergent central character young  actress shailene woodley  absolutely dazzled fans with her poise  ferocity  and stalwart courage after spending her  life with her family  firmly ensconced within the abnegation  faction  tris is totally unprepared for the  moment when she ends up with a deeply  confusing result  that says she's divergent in an effort  to hide her true nature  tris chooses to join the dauntless  faction jumping head first into a life  of adventure  thrills and bravery after already  appearing in prestige films like 2011's  the descendants and 2013's teen romance  the spectacular now  woodley continued her teen fare streak  after divergent hit the silver screen  2014 saw her star in the young adult  blockbuster  the fault in our stars along with the  divergent sequels  woodley popped up in projects like the  2016 biopic snowden before taking a  break from acting and coming back strong  in 2017 with a role on hbo's smash hit  miniseries  big little lies as assault survivor and  single mother  jane chapman with that woodley firmly  moved into more adult roles  winning accolades across the board she  followed it up with the buzzy survival  film adrift  in 2019 woodley made major news  in february 2021 when she announced her  engagement to superstar quarterback  aaron rodgers  when triss arrives in the dauntless  faction she's tested by tobias for eden  played by theo james an instructor who  is assigned to help new recruits  learn the skills of their chosen group  four is a tough teacher  are you kidding no  what makes you think you can talk to me  but he eventually takes a real liking to  triss  when tris is very nearly forced out of  the dauntless faction  due to her lack of skills four decides  to personally train her  but four isn't everything he appears to  be and ultimately he reveals his  shocking secret  he's actually the son of a strict  abnegation leader himself  this truth leads to a romantic  connection between him  and triss born and raised in england  james was best known for 2012's  underworld awakening  prior to his role in divergent alongside  reprising his role in insurgent and  allegiant  james appeared in the 2016 film the  benefactor  and in the underworld sequel blood wars  which hit movie theaters that same year  in the time since divergent debuted  james has shown up in a variety of  movies  including 2020's archive since 2015  james has also worked as an ambassador  for hugo boss  representing its men's collection of  fragrances  part of triss's struggle in joining the  dauntless faction it comes from having  to leave behind her family  losing her mother natalie who is played  by ashley judd  is an especially wrenching loss but  natalie isn't just a mother doing her  best  in impossible circumstances eventually  natalie reveals something shocking to  triss  she herself is also divergent and was  raised as a dauntless  as a result she understands better than  anybody that tris  is in serious danger by the time she  appeared in divergent  ashley judd was already famous she's  best known for her celebrated roles in a  wide variety of movies like 1995's heat  1996's a time to kill 1999's double  jeopardy  and 2000's where the heart is among many  others since divergent judd has taken on  fewer film roles  showing up in romantic comedies like  2014's  big stone gap and the 2016 barack obama  biopic  barry in 2017 she appeared on the twin  peaks reboot as beverly page  followed by a 2017 role on berlin  station  as bb yates she's also active  politically and socially  supporting a number of worthy causes in  2021 she experienced a serious injury  while researching  endangered bonobos in the congo  thankfully her recovery has gone well  over the course of her childhood in the  abnegation faction  tris enjoys a certain level of privilege  due to the fact that her father  andrew played by tony goldwyn is one of  the faction's leaders  because abnegation is in charge of the  government andrew is especially powerful  as a result he feels particularly  betrayed when triss doesn't choose  abnegation  for fans of scandal it was a true  delight to see goldwyn pop up in  divergent and insurgent  from 2012 to 2018 goldwyn played united  states president fitzgerald fitzgrant  throughout all seven seasons of shonda  rhimes's wonderfully soapy political  drama on abc  goldwyn is also an accomplished director  and stage actor  he's directed four feature films  including 2001's  someone like you 2010's conviction and  has appeared in several off-broadway  plays  and musicals since scandal and divergent  wrapped up  goldwyn has showed up on netflix's 2019  original series chambers alongside uma  thurman  and on hbo's 2020 science fiction epic  lovecraft country the fourth member of  the prior family  caleb pryor played by ansel elgort faces  a similar challenge  as tris does during his evaluation  should he stay with his loved ones and  abnegation  go with his sister daedauntless or seek  his own unique path  ultimately caleb bucks every trend and  chooses erudite alienating himself  from both his sister and his parents  shortly after appearing  as shailene woodley's brother in  divergent al gore shook things up by  reuniting with the actress  for 2014's the fault in our stars  in that film elgor plays augustus waters  the doomed love interest  to woodley's hazel grace elgor also  returned for both insurgent and  allegiant  in 2017 he earned his first major reward  knot  thanks to his starring role in edgar  wright's sleek action flick baby driver  which netted the actor a golden globe  nomination in 2018 he followed up baby  driver with billionaire boys club  and in 2019 he played the leading role  in the goldfinch the highly anticipated  adaptation  of donna tart's novel of the same name  which ended up being a major box office  flop  a violent and strong member of dauntless  who was raised in candor  peter is played by miles teller and is a  dangerous combination  of ruthlessness honesty and brutality  unsurprisingly he defeats trist in  hand-to-hand combat right off the bat  and also viciously attacks anyone who  ranks above him  before he was getting sinister and  divergent teller played opposite woodley  as her love interest  in 2013's the spectacular now alongside  the release of divergent  in 2014 he appeared in damien chazelle's  film  whiplash which earned a number of oscar  nots and a few wins  including one for teller's co-star j.k  simmons  he also appeared in two 2014 romantic  comedies  that awkward moment and two night stand  teller went on to appear in both  insurgent and allegiant as well as other  big budget films  like 2015's fantastic four indie  projects like 2016  get a job in searing dramas like 2017's  thank you  for your service dauntless's leaders  are some of the toughest and bravest  people in divergent's post-apocalyptic  world  this group includes jai courtney's eric  one of the faction's youngest ever  leaders  though eric is a high ranking official  amongst the dauntless  he certainly hasn't made many friends  throughout his tenure  acting unnecessarily cruel towards  trainees taking pleasure from their  failures and pain  and even helping erudite in their evil  mission  within the series courtney went on to  appear an insurgent before his turn as  eric hit the silver screen  courtney had a recurring role on star's  historical action  series spartacus blood and sand that's  not his only small screen success  he's also appeared on the 2017 netflix  reboot  wet hot american summer 10 years later  and 2020's  stateless you've also likely seen  courtney in some of his blockbuster  projects  including 2015's terminator genesis 2016  suicide squad 2019's elita battle angel  and 2020's honest thief  triss only makes a few friends when she  arrives in dauntless luckily they turn  out to be stalwart allies  like zoe kravitz's christina who proves  to be extremely important throughout the  entire series  another dauntless transplant christina  is smart and industrious  but usually suffers in hand-to-hand  combat though she and triss occasionally  butt heads they always team up together  the divergent films were just the start  of a lengthy and fruitful collaboration  between kravitz and woodley  who in 2017 would appear as two of the  leading ladies of hbo's star-studded  miniseries  big little lies kravitz plays a young  yoga teacher  named bonnie whose calm exterior is  shattered by a shocking suburban  murderer  kravitz has appeared in a ton of other  projects as well  including the short-lived 2020 hulu  reboot of high fidelity  which in a modern twist cast her as john  cusack's character rob  renamed robin she also appeared as letty  lestrange in 2018's fantastic beasts  the crimes of grindelwald one of  immortan joe's wives  in 2015's mad max fury road and as the  one and only catwoman in matt reeves  2022 reboot  of the batman film franchise when tris  first takes her personality test and  gets the surprising result that she is  divergent  only one person initially knows about it  dauntless member tori wu  played by maggie q shocked by the result  tori immediately warns tris that being  marked as divergent is extraordinarily  dangerous  they call it divergent  you can't tell anyone about this not  even your parents tori is the first  person to tell tris that those marked  divergent can destroy the entire system  gives her vital information and  ultimately joins her fellow dauntless  in the climactic fight against erudite  during her time in the divergent movies  q also starred in the title role on the  cw's nikita series which ran until 2013  as well as the short-lived 2014 series  stalker on which she had the main role  the actress was also a series regular as  hannah wells on designated survivor  from 2016 to 2019 and has appeared in  recent movies like 2020's fantasy island  2020's death of me in 2021's the protege  she has also explored voice acting most  prominently in the role of wonder woman  on young justice one of the older  leaders of the dauntless faction  makai pfeiffer's max has given all of  his responsibilities to eric  by the time divergent begins despite the  fact that he wanted  four to follow in his footsteps though  max isn't quite as cruel as eric  he's also not an ally to triss or any of  the dauntless rebels  pfeiffer was already a popular actor by  the time he appeared in divergent  and its sequels he is likely best known  for his work with spike lee in 1995's  clockers  and for his six-year stint on the  popular medical series  er over the years pfeiffer has carved  out a solid career  on the small screen appearing on shows  like white collar frequency  and the 2020 hulu original series love  victor  the leader of the erudite faction kate  winslet's jeanine has a dark past  janine also developed the personality  test that helps sort the young people  choosing their new or old factions  i think human nature is the enemy  it's human nature to keep secrets lie to  steal  and i want to eradicate that she's  additionally responsible for something  much more sinister  a mind control serum that the erudite  attempt to use to destroy the dauntless  faction  as most moviegoers know winslet was  already a superstar  when she took on the villainous role of  janine in both divergent and insurgent  winslet is internationally renowned for  her starring roles in huge projects like  1997's titanic  2004's eternal sunshine of the spotless  mind 2008's revolutionary road  and 2008's the reader which won winslet  her first academy award  since divergent winslet has peered and  acclaimed movies like the 2015 biopic  steve jobs the intense 2017 survival  film the mountain between us  and the 2020 romantic drama ammonite  abnegation is supposed to be the  selfless faction but one of its leaders  marcus eaton played by ray stevenson is  an abusive and cruel man  his behavior drives evelyn into the  world without a faction  and four into escaping abnegation in  favor of dauntless  a veteran of both the big and small  screen stevenson was the perfect choice  to portray  the austere inscrutable marcus long  before his work in divergent  stevenson was known for his leading  roles in 2004's king arthur  and the epic hbo series rome he's also  beloved by superhero fans for his turns  as frank castle  better known as the punisher in 2008's  punisher warzone  and volstag an asgardian warrior and one  of thor's dearest friends  in the first three thor films during his  time in the divergent film series  stevenson also showed up on shows like  dexter and black sails  in the movies aftermath the actor has  taken on roles in historical dramas like  medici  the spanish princess and vikings check  out one of our news videos right here  plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite sci-fi gems are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one
 

